<Layout title="Manage your website — Life as Sakti"><section class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">YOUR WRITING DESK</p><h1>A home for<br/><em>your next idea.</em></h1><p class="intro">Write and edit articles, upload images, and update your website in a visual editor.</p><a class="button" href="https://app.pagescms.org/">Open website editor ↗</a><p class="muted">Sign in with GitHub and choose sakti1977 / saktibagchiblog.</p></section><section class="manage-guide"><h2>From idea to published article</h2><ol><li><strong>Write.</strong> Open Blog posts and create an entry. Keep the draft switch on while working.</li><li><strong>Add the details.</strong> Choose a publication date, permanent web address, cover image, topics, and a short summary.</li><li><strong>Review.</strong> Use the visual editor to check your text. A full website preview workflow is still being configured.</li><li><strong>Publish.</strong> Turn off the draft switch and save. Once automatic deployment is connected, Railway rebuilds the website.</li></ol><p>Existing article addresses should stay unchanged so bookmarked links keep working.</p><p><strong>Draft privacy:</strong> this repository is currently public. Drafts are hidden from the website, but their saved files are visible on GitHub. Use a private repository before storing confidential drafts.</p><p><strong>Setup status:</strong> GitHub authorization for Pages CMS and the first publish test still need to be completed.</p></section></Layout>
